        "text": "A broker resumes with PermitAuthority(ledger_path) on the edited file described in \"ledger\". What does the constructor raise? Give the exact PermitError code."
      },
      {
        "id": "code",
        "hash": "f8f07aa2d81b360ae0f916ee62a9cd30a0bfa99731c43d8597a9e8e5a92f3b2f",
        "text": "    def __init__(self, path: Path | None):\n        ...\n        if self.path is not None and self.path.exists():\n            for event in self.read():\n                self._last = event[\"event_hash\"]\n    ...\n        events, previous = [], None\n        with self.path.open(encoding=\"utf-8\") as stream:\n            for number, line in enumerate(stream, 1):\n                event = json.loads(line)\n                unsigned = {k: v for k, v in event.items() if k != \"event_hash\"}\n                require(event.get(\"previous_event_hash\") == previous, f\"ledger_chain_broken_line_{number}\")\n                require(digest(unsigned) == event.get(\"event_hash\"), f\"ledger_hash_mismatch_line_{number}\")\n                events.append(event)\n                previous = event[\"event_hash\"]\n        return events\n    ...\n        try:\n            self.ledger = HashChainLedger(ledger_path)\n        except PermitError:\n            raise\n        except Exception as exc:\n            raise PermitError(\"ledger_unreadable\") from exc"
      },
      {
        "id": "ledger",
        "hash": "8bd635c0a4e0ef7f73006116a19759aed161d00826bf428e17dca83364988d02",
        "text": "Original permits.jsonl, four lines, each written by append() (event_hash = SHA-256 of the line without event_hash; previous_event_hash = the previous line's event_hash):\nline 1: permit_issued p-1, previous_event_hash null, event_hash H1\nline 2: permit_consumed p-1, previous_event_hash H1, event_hash H2\nline 3: permit_receipt p-1, previous_event_hash H2, event_hash H3\nline 4: permit_issued p-2, previous_event_hash H3, event_hash H4\nSomeone deletes line 2 with a text editor and saves. Nothing else changes."
      }
